es for the Veterans Health Administration of the Department\nof Veterans Affairs (38 U.S.C. 7306, 7404; section 301(a) of Public Law\n102–40) at Schedule 3.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Senior Executive Service. The ranges of rates of basic pay for senior\nexecutives in the Senior Executive Service, as established pursuant to 5\nU.S.C. 5382, are set forth on Schedule 4 attached hereto and made a part\nhereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 2","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Certain Executive, Legislative and Judicial Salaries. The rates of\nbasic pay or salaries for the following offices and positions are set forth\non the schedules attached hereto and made a part hereof:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Executive Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5312–5318) at Schedule 5;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Vice President (3 U.S.C. 104) and the Congress (2 U.S.C. 31)\nat Schedule 6; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Justices and judges (28 U.S.C. 5, 44(d), 135, 252, and 461(a), section\n140 of Public Law 97–92, and section 306 of Division B of Public Law\n108–447) at Schedule 7.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Uniformed Services. Pursuant to section 601(a)–(b) of Public Law\n108–375, the rates of monthly basic pay (37 U.S.C. 203(a)) for members\nof the uniformed services, as adjusted under 37 U.S.C. 1009, and the rate\nof monthly cadet or midshipman pay (37 U.S.C. 203(c)) are set forth on\nSchedule 8 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 4","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Pursuant to section 5304\nof title 5, United States Code, and section 640 of Division H of Public\nLaw 108–447, locality-based comparability payments shall be paid in accord-\nance with Schedule 9 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Director of the Office of Personnel Management shall take such\nactions as may be necessary to implement these payments and to publish\nappropriate notice of such payments in the Federal Register.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 5(b)","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec5(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 6. Administrative Law Judges. The rates of basic pay for administrative\nlaw judges, as adjusted under 5 U.S.C. 5372(b)(4), are set forth on Schedule\n10 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 6","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec6","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 7. Effective Dates. Schedule 8 is effective on January 1, 2005. The\nother schedules contained herein are effective on the first day of the first\napplicable pay period beginning on or after January 1, 2005.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 1147 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 7","sha256":"6c8ccaebd66d8b92164adf13ecc6884162347fe5212b7fe99702581e7d094de1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-05/pdf/05-306.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13368#sec7","state_at_cutoff":null},{"curr